BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Bozcaada//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Bozcaada — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Çavuş\, the dry white — The island’s big pale table grape\, made into a dry white wine.
DESCRIPTION:Say: chah-VOOSH. A grape most of the world only eats\, here made into wine\; the table grape itself is a registered GI. Best: The tasting counter at Talay’s shop\, Lale Sokak\, in town
LOCATION:The tasting counter at Talay’s shop\, Lale Sokak\, in town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Talay+%C5%9Earap%C3%A7%C4%B1l%C4%B1k+Lale+Sokak+5+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vasilaki — The island’s other white grape: crisp\, high in acid.
DESCRIPTION:Say: vah-see-LAH-kee. One of the four grapes the island grows and almost nobody else does. Best: Talay’s shop in town\, from the family’s own vines
LOCATION:Talay’s shop in town\, from the family’s own vines
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Talay+%C5%9Earap%C3%A7%C4%B1l%C4%B1k+Lale+Sokak+5+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Karalahna — The island’s dark\, tannic red grape.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kah-rah-LAH-nah. The red to taste beside Kuntra\, to learn the island’s two reds. Best: Talay’s shop in town
LOCATION:Talay’s shop in town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Talay+%C5%9Earap%C3%A7%C4%B1l%C4%B1k+Lale+Sokak+5+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kuntra — The island’s lighter red grape.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KOON-trah. Talay blends it with Cabernet: taste the blend and the native grape in one glass. Best: Talay’s Cabernet Sauvignon–Kuntra\, at the shop in town
LOCATION:Talay’s Cabernet Sauvignon–Kuntra\, at the shop in town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Talay+%C5%9Earap%C3%A7%C4%B1l%C4%B1k+Lale+Sokak+5+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Corpus — Corvus’s flagship red\, about two-thirds Cabernet\, from the estate at Tuzburnu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KOR-poos. The bottle that made the island a name in serious wine. Best: Corvus\, at the estate\; visiting has been summer-only\, so ask first
LOCATION:Corvus\, at the estate\; visiting has been summer-only\, so ask first
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Corvus+Ba%C4%9Fc%C4%B1l%C4%B1k+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rakı — The anise spirit\, poured with cold water so it turns milky\, drunk slowly with the meze.
DESCRIPTION:Say: rah-KUH. Not an island product\, but the island’s meal: the wine is the souvenir\, the rakı is dinner. Best: Under the vine at Asmalı Meyhane
LOCATION:Under the vine at Asmalı Meyhane
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Asmal%C4%B1+Meyhane+%C3%87%C4%B1nar+%C3%87ar%C5%9F%C4%B1+Caddesi+20+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kalamar on the coals — Island squid grilled plain over charcoal\, not battered.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kah-lah-MAR. The way the island has cooked its squid since before the fried mainland version. Best: Asmalı Meyhane\, Çınar Çarşı Caddesi
LOCATION:Asmalı Meyhane\, Çınar Çarşı Caddesi
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Asmal%C4%B1+Meyhane+%C3%87%C4%B1nar+%C3%87ar%C5%9F%C4%B1+Caddesi+20+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Raw fish with basil — Raw fish dressed with torn basil\, the quiet plate of the meyhane.
DESCRIPTION:Say: . The meyhane’s second signature\, beside the squid. Best: Asmalı Meyhane
LOCATION:Asmalı Meyhane
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Asmal%C4%B1+Meyhane+%C3%87%C4%B1nar+%C3%87ar%C5%9F%C4%B1+Caddesi+20+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Sandal borani — The house borani of Sandal\, a cold yoghurt meze named for the restaurant.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sahn-DAHL bo-rah-NEE. Eaten in what was the island’s old coffeehouse\, on the street that was its bazaar. Best: Sandal\, Alsancak Sokak
LOCATION:Sandal\, Alsancak Sokak
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sandal+Restaurant+Alsancak+Sokak+31+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Damla sakızlı enginar — Artichoke scented with mastic\, a cold meze.
DESCRIPTION:Say: dahm-LAH sah-kuz-LUH en-gee-NAR. Mastic\, the Aegean resin\, in a savoury plate: the island’s Greek pantry in one bite. Best: Sandal\, Alsancak Sokak
LOCATION:Sandal\, Alsancak Sokak
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sandal+Restaurant+Alsancak+Sokak+31+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bozcaada Bombası — Nevreste’s stuffed house meze\, the plate reviewers name first.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boz-JAH-ah-dah BOM-bah-suh. Made by one house only. Best: Nevreste\, Alsancak Sokak
LOCATION:Nevreste\, Alsancak Sokak
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nevreste+Alsancak+Sokak+22+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mantı — Small hand-pinched dumplings under garlic yoghurt and chilli butter.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mahn-TUH. The home-cooking plate of the island\, made by hand in a family kitchen. Best: Dört Hanımeli\, in town
LOCATION:Dört Hanımeli\, in town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=D%C3%B6rt+Han%C4%B1meli+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Enginarlı ahtapot — Octopus and artichoke in a cream sauce with rosemary.
DESCRIPTION:Say: en-gee-nar-LUH ah-tah-POT. What an island cook does with the island’s two best ingredients. Best: Ada’m\, Alsancak Sokak
LOCATION:Ada’m\, Alsancak Sokak
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Adam+Restaurant+Alsancak+Sokak+42+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Domates reçeli — Tomato jam\, cooked in late summer and sold by the jar.
DESCRIPTION:Say: do-MAH-tes reh-cheh-LEE. Sweet against salty white cheese: the island’s best-known preserve. Best: The weekly market\, by the jar
LOCATION:The weekly market\, by the jar
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bozcaada+pazar%C4%B1+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Çavuş grapes\, fresh — The registered table grape\, big and pale gold\, eaten off the bunch.
DESCRIPTION:Say: chah-VOOSH. Only in late summer: if you are here at harvest\, this is the taste of the island. Best: The weekly market\, in season
LOCATION:The weekly market\, in season
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bozcaada+pazar%C4%B1+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bademli kurabiye — The mastic-almond cookie of the Rum kitchen\, baked in a wood-fired oven.
DESCRIPTION:Say: bah-dem-LEE koo-rah-bee-YEH. A Greek recipe still made on the island\, and on Gökçeada and in Kavala. Best: Çiçek Pastanesi
LOCATION:Çiçek Pastanesi
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87i%C3%A7ek+Pastanesi+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:bozcaada-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mastic ice cream — Dondurma flavoured with mastic resin\, from the pastane’s counter.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sah-KUZ-luh don-door-MAH. Chase the wild-fig one too when the island’s figs are in. Best: Çiçek Pastanesi\, in summer
LOCATION:Çiçek Pastanesi\, in summer
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87i%C3%A7ek+Pastanesi+Bozcaada+%C3%87anakkale+T%C3%BCrkiye
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
